  "title": "Density of Symmetric Primes",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Given pairs of odd primes $p, q$, define $S(q,p)$ as the number of lattice points $(m, n)$ in the rectangle $0 < m < p/2$, $0 < n < q/2$ below the diagonal. A pair is symmetric if $S(p, q) = S(q,p)$. Is the number of symmetric primes less than $x$ equal to $x/(\\ln x)^{\\sigma+o(1)}$, where $\\sigma = 2 - (1+\\ln \\ln 2)/\\ln 2 \\approx 1.08607$?",
